WEBVTT

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:05.580
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me over that fan?</v>

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:13.240
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, just about. Whose new car's that in the car park? Taking up a very generous interpretation of one space.</v>

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.649
<v David Whitfield>Not mine. Mine's the one with more primer than paint.</v>

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.230
<v Marcus Hale>Ah, the two-tone executive model.</v>

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:30.719
<v Fiona Doyle>Never mind the car, the coffee machine in the canteen's still broken. Just an observation, before anyone gives me that as a job.</v>

00:00:31.559 --> 00:00:34.710
<v Tomasz Nowak>The hot water tasted better than the coffee anyway.</v>

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:42.270
<v Hannah Price>I've got a walking weekend planned and the weather looks absolutely grim. Broken coffee machine's really setting the mood.</v>

00:00:43.159 --> 00:00:48.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Well, it's only Tuesday, 20 October. Plenty of time for the forecast to get worse.</v>

00:00:50.439 --> 00:00:53.590
<v Fiona Doyle>That's the motivational bit of the meeting done, then.</v>

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:59.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Finished work first, then what's actually going on the list.</v>

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:06.939
<v Marcus Hale>I signed off the inspection on the compressor one on Tuesday—this morning, I mean. That's done.</v>

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, closed, not another inspection today.</v>

00:01:13.549 --> 00:01:19.849
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same here: signed off the inspection on the gas turbine one on Tuesday, earlier this morning. All finished.</v>

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:29.310
<v Fiona Doyle>And we finished the repair on the GT2 inlet valve last night. That's a completion update, not something still waiting.</v>

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.859
<v David Whitfield>Right, that was the one I thought was still open. Good.</v>

00:01:37.019 --> 00:01:39.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Those are all in the done column, then.</v>

00:01:41.989 --> 00:01:49.340
<v Tomasz Nowak>Um, I saw the pressure on the Line 3 Chiller dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.480
<v David Whitfield>Stayed back up, or was it hunting?</v>

00:01:55.230 --> 00:02:01.180
<v Tomasz Nowak>Stayed back up while I was there. Just passing on what I saw, not raising a repair.</v>

00:02:01.739 --> 00:02:10.139
<v Fiona Doyle>Similar observation here: saw the pressure on the palletizer dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own. Nothing ongoing to report.</v>

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, observations only. Neither of those is a new job from this meeting.</v>

00:02:16.389 --> 00:02:21.990
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Still waiting on parts for the line 2 interlock, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.719
<v Sarah Okafor>So that remains blocked, not something we're pretending we can finish today.</v>

00:02:29.719 --> 00:02:35.319
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Exactly. And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the trucks. Same uncertainty as before.</v>

00:02:36.139 --> 00:02:41.740
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, there's no confirmed delivery in the schedule. It's still a blocker, not a booked slot.</v>

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:45.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Those stay as blocked items.</v>

00:02:47.629 --> 00:02:55.330
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the relief valve. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:01.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, Tomasz Nowak owns that. The relief valve permit and isolation come first.</v>

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:08.849
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, I'll take it. No point putting the other bits ahead of that.</v>

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:16.069
<v Sarah Okafor>And Tomasz, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the feedwater pump tomorrow morning? Top priority please.</v>

00:03:18.169 --> 00:03:22.719
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yes, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the feedwater pump tomorrow morning.</v>

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:30.860
<v Sarah Okafor>Just to keep that straight: relief valve first because production's held up; feedwater pump sign-off is top priority tomorrow morning.</v>

00:03:32.349 --> 00:03:35.150
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, understood. Those two aren't getting muddled together.</v>

00:03:37.569 --> 00:03:45.969
<v Sarah Okafor>There's also a site visit at the substation with the contractor needing doing by Thursday. Lower down the pile—if you've got a spare minute.</v>

00:03:46.389 --> 00:03:53.740
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll do a site visit at the substation with the contractor by Thursday. I can take that as the lower-priority one.</v>

00:03:56.039 --> 00:03:59.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tom. By Thursday, but not ahead of those priority jobs.</v>

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.770
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's fine. A spare-minute job, but Thursday still stands.</v>

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:12.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you run a function test on the line 2 guard by Wednesday, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:22.209
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll run a function test on the line 2 guard by Wednesday. Fit that in when I get a chance.</v>

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:30.199
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, talking over you—just keeping the names separate. The blocked parts item I mentioned is the line 2 interlock.</v>

00:04:31.279 --> 00:04:36.529
<v Hannah Price>Yep, understood. I've accepted the line 2 guard function test, not the blocked interlock work.</v>

00:04:37.879 --> 00:04:42.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Easy to lose that distinction when Teams chops half a sentence off.</v>

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:52.639
<v Olumide Adeyemi>While we're on the quieter stuff, I'll sort the training records for the new starters by the end of the week. No rush on that one.</v>

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:59.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Olumide Adeyemi. Training records with you, by the end of the week, no rush.</v>

00:05:01.329 --> 00:05:05.180
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep. It's the records I'm sorting, not adding any training sessions.</v>

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:14.209
<v Sarah Okafor>Olumide Adeyemi, can I give you the monthly fire alarm test this afternoon as well? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:15.819 --> 00:05:24.220
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Not that one, sorry. I haven't got the capacity this afternoon. I can keep the records, but I can't take the fire alarm test.</v>

00:05:25.569 --> 00:05:32.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Dave, can you take it instead—run the monthly fire alarm test this afternoon? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:33.339 --> 00:05:38.240
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll take that instead. I'll run the monthly fire alarm test this afternoon.</v>

00:05:40.149 --> 00:05:44.350
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, that's a handover, not two people down for the same test.</v>

00:05:45.319 --> 00:05:48.470
<v David Whitfield>One of me's quite enough, according to most people.</v>

00:05:49.199 --> 00:05:58.649
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah so, I'll order spare parts for the pick and place on two by Wednesday. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:06:00.839 --> 00:06:06.089
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Marcus. Spare parts for the pick and place on two with you, by Wednesday.</v>

00:06:06.819 --> 00:06:12.069
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll get the order in. We're talking ordering the spares, not promising a repair.</v>

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:16.600
<v Fiona Doyle>Got it. Wednesday is the order deadline, not a delivery date.</v>

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:26.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's the agreed work. The line 2 interlock parts and the trucks delivery are still blockers; no extra chasing job being handed out here.</v>

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:31.610
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Correct. Nothing's magically arrived while we've been talking.</v>

00:06:32.339 --> 00:06:38.639
<v Hannah Price>Neither has any sunshine, judging by that window. My weekend plan might just become sitting in a pub.</v>

00:06:39.759 --> 00:06:41.860
<v David Whitfield>A robust weather contingency. Sound engineering.</v>

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:47.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this turns into a design review of the pub—thanks, everyone. That's us.</v>

00:06:48.709 --> 00:06:49.910
<v Tomasz Nowak>Cheers.</v>

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:52.699
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, all.</v>
